WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
This video shows what you are trying to do

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.320
when you perform CPR.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.800
When someone's heart stops beating properly,

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.620
their body stops moving blood on its own.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.640
Blood is what carries oxygen to the brain and other organs.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.040
When you push on the chest,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.240
you are taking over the heart's job.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.040
Your hands work like a pump.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.280
Each push moves blood through the body

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.799
and helps keep the person alive until EMS arrives.

00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:26.400
Here is a key point.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.160
The person's blood already has oxygen in it at first.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.160
The problem is not a lack of oxygen right away.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.220
The problem is that the oxygen is not moving.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.160
Chest compressions push that oxygen-filled blood

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.240
to the brain.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.160
Protecting the brain is why compressions matter most

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.439
in the first few minutes.

